===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The act of [[connect]]ing.
# The point at which two or more things are connected.
#: {{ux|en|the '''connection''' between overeating and obesity}}
#: {{ux|en|My headache has no '''connection''' with me going out last night.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=April 15, 2004|title=Morning swoop in hunt for Jodi's killer|work=The Scotsman|url=http://www.scotsman.com/news/morning_swoop_in_hunt_for_jodi_s_killer_1_521912|passage=A spokesman for Lothian and Borders Police said: "We can confirm that a 15-year-old boy has been arrested and charged in connection with the murder of Jodi Jones. A 45-year-old has also been arrested in '''connection''' with allegations of attempting to pervert the course of justice. A report on this has been sent to the procurator fiscal."}}
# A feeling of [[understanding]] and [[ease]] of [[communication]] between two or more people.
#: {{ux|en|As we were the only people in the room to laugh at the joke, I felt a '''connection''' between us.}}
# An [[established]] [[communications]] or [[transportation]] link.
#: {{ux|en|computers linked by a network '''connection'''}}
#: {{ux|en|I was talking to him, but there was lightning and we lost the '''connection'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The Route 4 bus will arrive on 5th St. at Robinson Ave at 3:30. The northbound number 14 is scheduled to arrive on Robinson at 3:31. That means you have to run across the street once you arrive, it's a spot '''connection'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transport}} A [[transfer]] from one transportation vehicle to another in scheduled transportation service.
#: {{ux|en|The bus was late so he missed his '''connection''' at Penn Station and had to wait six hours for the next train.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 January 12|author=Paul Bigland|title=Fab Four: the nation's finest stations: Eastbourne|journal=RAIL|issue=948|page=26|text=It is kept super-clean by helpful staff who still find the time to help customers with tight '''connections'''.}}
# A [[kinship]] [[relationship]] between people.
# A person related to oneself, through either [[family]] or [[business]].
#: {{ux|en|I have some '''connections''' in Lancashire.}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} A [[set]] of sets that contains the [[empty set]], all one-element sets for any element that is included in any of the sets, and the [[union]] of any group of sets that are elements where the intersections of those sets is non-empty.
# [[coherence|Coherence]]; lack of [[disjointedness]].
# {{label|en|religion}} A [[Methodist]] denomination as a whole, as opposed to its [[constituent]] [[church]]es, [[circuit]]s, [[district]]s and [[conference]]s.
# [[sexual intercourse|Sexual intercourse]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1927|author=Havelock Ellis|title=Studies in the Psychology of Sex, Volume 2 (of 6)|chapter=|edition=|url=http://www.gutenberg.org/files/13611/13611-h/13611-h.htm|passage=The exact nature of the relations between the boy-wife and his protector are doubtful; they certainly have '''connection''', but the natives repudiate with horror and disgust the idea of sodomy.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1941|author=George Ryley Scott|authorlink=George Ryley Scott|title=Phallic Worship: A History of Sex and Sex Rites in Relation to the Religions of All Races from Antiquity to the Present Day|publisher=T. Werner Laurie|location=London|page=29|passage=At the town of Mendes, in the principal temple, there was a living male goat, with which, if the statement of Herodotus is to be accepted, naked female worshippers actually had carnal intercourse. Male worshippers similarly had '''connexion''' with she-goats.}}
# {{senseid|en|dealer}} {{lb|en|slang}} A [[drug dealer]].
#* {{RQ:Kerouac On the Road|passage=Now the final study was the drug habit. He was now in New Orleans, slipping along the streets with shady characters and haunting '''connection''' bars.}}

